0000:                   *******************************************
0000:                   * PTY
0000:                   *  Device Driver for emulated terminal
0000:                   * Emulates the 6850 UART seen in usim
0000:                   *
0000:                   * V.port is the control (write) / status (read) port, V.port+1 is the data port:
0000:                   *  status bit 0: 1=received character ready (RDRF)
0000:                   *         bit 1: 1=ready for output (TDRE)
0000:                   *         bit 7: 1=the ACIA requests an interrupt
0000:                   *  control bit 7: receive interrupt enable (RIE)
0000:                   *          bits 6-5 = 01: transmit interrupt enable (TIE)
0000:                   *          bits 1-0 = 11: master reset
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Both directions are interrupt driven (the ACIA of sim09 and of the FPGA board raises IRQ):
0000:                   *  - the interrupt service routine (entered with F$IRQ, called by the Clock module through D.Poll)
0000:                   *    puts every received character in a ring buffer of 128 bytes, so that input is not lost while no
0000:                   *    process reads and the keyboard interrupt / quit / pause characters work at once (the signal goes
0000:                   *    to the last process that used the terminal), even for a program that never reads;
0000:                   *  - output goes through a ring buffer of 64 bytes, emptied by the transmit interrupt: the process
0000:                   *    continues while the characters are sent.  When the transmitter is idle a character goes out directly.
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Edition History
0000:                   *
0000:                   * #   date     Comments
0000:                   * - -------- -------------------------------
0000:                   * 1 16.11.01  Driver first written (polled). SMR
0000:                   * 2 26.11.05  Interrupt driven: receive and transmit rings, F$IRQ, ^C ^E ^W at once, SS.Ready counts
0000:                   
0000:                            nam PTY
0000:                            ttl Pseudo Terminal
0000:                   
0000:                            ifp1
0000:                            use defsfile
0000:                            endc
0000:                   
0002:                   Revision equ 2
0000:                   
0000:                   * 6850 bits
0001:                   St.RxF   equ   $01              receive data register full
0002:                   St.TxE   equ   $02              transmit data register empty
0080:                   St.IRQ   equ   $80              interrupt request
0003:                   Cr.Rst   equ   $03              master reset
0015:                   Cr.Base  equ   $15              divide by 16, 8 bits, no parity, 1 stop bit (no interrupts)
0080:                   Cr.RIE   equ   $80              receive interrupt enable
0020:                   Cr.TIE   equ   $20              transmit interrupt enable (with bit 6 = 0)
0000:                   
0000:                   * the static storage must stay within one page (256 bytes): on Level 1 a second page splits the free memory and jwp would not f
001D:                   it
0080:                   RxSize   equ   128              receive ring (a power of 2)
007F:                   RxMask   equ   RxSize-1
0040:                   TxSize   equ   64               transmit ring (a power of 2)
003F:                   TxMask   equ   TxSize-1
0000:                   
0000:                            org V.SCF
001D:                   RxHead   rmb 1                  receive ring: where the ISR puts the next character
001E:                   RxTail   rmb 1                  where READ takes the next one
001F:                   TxHead   rmb 1                  transmit ring: where WRITE puts the next character
0020:                   TxTail   rmb 1                  where the ISR takes the next one
0021:                   CtlShd   rmb 1                  the control register (it cannot be read)
0022:                   RxBuf    rmb RxSize
00A2:                   TxBuf    rmb TxSize
00E2:                   PST      equ .
00E2:                   
